#############################################################################
# bianchi_d7_lowindex.g
#
# PSL_2(O_{-7}) low-index subgroup experiment -- SKELETON, DO NOT RUN YET.
#
# REQUIRES: a verified d=-7 presentation copied directly from
# Grunewald & Schwermer, "Subgroups of Bianchi groups and arithmetic
# quotients of hyperbolic 3-space", Trans. Amer. Math. Soc. 335(1), 1993,
# pp. 47-78. Do not reconstruct the relators from memory or a relayed
# summary -- copy them from the source table.
#
# The companion presentation for the extended/maximal arithmetic overgroup
# (needed for Stage 2 below) is not yet sourced at all as of 2026-08-25.
#
# PURPOSE
# -------
# Stage 1 (control): enumerate index <= 6 subgroups of the ORDINARY
#   T7 = PSL_2(O_{-7}). Independently verified this session:
#     covol(T7) = 0.888914927816353  (Humbert volume formula, computed
#     directly via Sage/PARI, not taken from any relay)
#     vol(m009) = vol(m010) = 2.66674478344906
#     2.66674478344906 / 0.888914927816353 = 3.000000... exactly
#   Grunewald-Schwermer's torsion obstruction requires any torsion-free
#   finite-index subgroup of T7 to have index divisible by 6. Since the
#   volume ratio forces index 3 for a literal embedding, m009/m010 CANNOT
#   be subgroups of ordinary T7 -- this stage exists to confirm that
#   deduction computationally (all index-3 classes should show torsion)
#   and to see what index-6 torsion-free classes exist as a control, not
#   as a target (they'd have volume ~5.333, not ~2.667).
#
# Stage 2 (target, NOT YET RUNNABLE): repeat against the maximal discrete
#   arithmetic extension of T7, predicted covolume ~0.44445746 (i.e.
#   covol(T7)/2), which would put m009/m010 at index 6 in that extension.
#
# CANDIDATE for the Stage 2 group, status as of 2026-08-25:
#   B7 = PGL_2(O_{-7}), realized inside PSL_2(C) via determinant-rescaling
#   of representatives, generated by T7 plus one projective involution
#   J: z -> -z (a determinant -1 class), J^2 = 1.
#
#   What's independently confirmed (computed directly in Sage, not taken
#   from any relay):
#     class_number(Q(sqrt(-7))) = 1
#     unit_group(O_{-7}) = C2 (order 2, i.e. {+-1})
#     => O_K^x / (O_K^x)^2 = C2, so [PGL_2(O_K) : PSL_2(O_K)] = 2 is
#        elementary algebra, independent of any external source.
#     covol(B7) = covol(T7)/2 = 0.444457463908...  (follows immediately
#        from the index-2 fact above and the already-verified covol(T7))
#     2.666744783449.../0.444457463908... = 6.000000... exactly, so IF
#        m009/m010 embed in this group, the index-6 prediction is
#        internally consistent.
#
#   What is NOT independently confirmed: that PGL_2(O_{-7}) actually
#   equals Vulakh's B_d (his maximal discrete extension of PSL_2(O_d) in
#   PSL_2(C)) -- i.e. that PGL_2(O_{-7}) is truly MAXIMAL, not just A
#   discrete extension. The elementary index-2 argument above shows
#   PGL_2(O_K) is *a* valid discrete extension; it does not by itself
#   prove nothing larger exists. Citation checked and real: L. Ya.
#   Vulakh, "Reflections in extended Bianchi groups," Math. Proc.
#   Cambridge Philos. Soc. 115(1), 1994, DOI 10.1017/S0305004100071887
#   (confirmed via Cambridge's own listing: real title, real author,
#   real journal/year -- but the fetched abstract describes reflection/
#   Coxeter subgroups and Vinberg's class-number-divides-4 criterion,
#   not a verbatim "B_d = PGL_2(O_d)" statement; the paper's full text
#   was not read, so the maximality claim itself is plausible/consistent
#   with standard theory, not confirmed against Vulakh's actual theorem).
#
#   Explicit 2x2 matrix generators and relators for either T7 or B7 have
#   NOT been sourced. Two candidate sources for T7, both checked to be
#   real and correctly attributed (an earlier relay's "Dinakaran (2022)"
#   attribution is confirmed FALSE -- no such paper exists):
#     - Grunewald & Schwermer, Trans. Amer. Math. Soc. 335(1), 1993,
#       pp. 47-78 (see header above)
#     - Tanner Reese, "Presentations for singly-cusped Bianchi groups,"
#       arXiv:2206.01262 (2022) AND the published version, Topology
#       Appl. 328 (2023), article 108443, DOI 10.1016/j.topol.2023.108443
#       -- confirmed via Crossref metadata, real, both attributed solely
#       to Tanner Reese. Covers PSL_2(O_d) for d=-7 explicitly, per its
#       own abstract -- but is about the ORDINARY group, not the
#       extended/PGL_2 group, so it is a candidate source for T7's
#       presentation only, not a ready-made Stage 2 presentation.
#   Neither paper's full text has been read (no institutional access;
#   piracy routes are not something this project will use). Do not fill
#   in the generator/relator TODOs below by guessing.
#
#############################################################################

SetInfoLevel(InfoWarning, 1);

########################################################################
# 1. PRESENTATION -- NOT YET FILLED IN
########################################################################

